 "title": "Psychological Reasons Behind Getting Ghosted",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains the three psychological reasons why people get ghosted in sales or professional outreach, which include being too desperate, taking ghosting personally, and making it awkward to reconnect. He advises keeping follow-ups calm, avoiding blame, and always keeping the door open for future communication.",
 "key_points": [
  "Being too desperate: Bombarding someone with endless messages and back-to-back calls when they are busy in a meeting will make them avoid you entirely.",
  "The creator points out that the person is likely just in a meeting they wanted to be in and would have replied later.",
  "Taking ghosting personally: Understand that ghosting is usually not about you, but because you are not yet relevant enough in their life.",
  "You need to follow up enough times using nice triggers that don't overwhelm them.",
  "Making it awkward to reconnect: People get embarrassed to get back on a call if they have ghosted you multiple times.",
  "Make sure you keep the door open even when closing an interaction by saying something like 'Hey listen, it's okay...'"
 ],
 "content": "This Is Why You're Getting Ghosted! I want you to understand the psychological problem behind ghosting. Three things! Either you have bombarded him on f*cking messages, call him back to back! Harass this guy! He probably was in a meeting buddy, and probably in a meeting that he wanted to be in and he would have gotten back to you. Now he has seen you harass the living f*ck out of him, so he's not calling you back or picking you a call in the future. Number two, don't take ghosting personally. It's probably not because of you, because you're not that relevant in his life. You just need to follow up enough time. So there's triggers you need to be able to pull in a nice way, which doesn't make them lose their mind. Third one! People are embarrassed so they don't want to get back on a call because they're like they've ghosted you three times! Make sure you keep the door open even if you're closing it, be like, hey listen, it's okay... Text: This Is Why You're Getting Ghosted! 1. Being Too Desperate. 2. Taking Ghosting Personally. 3. Making It Awkward to Reconnect / Blaming them for missing calls instead of making it easy to reconnect.",
